[44.203, "o", "   {\"answer\":\"I'm not a doctor, but the LiveWell guides suggest: use the healthy plate-1/2 vegetables and fruit, 1/4 wholegrains or staples, and 1/4 protein such as fish, chicken, tofu, eggs or beans. Choose brown rice, oats or wholemeal bread more often; keep rice/noodle portions sensible; spread carbohydrates across the day; and pair them with vegetables and protein. Choose water, kopi kosong or teh siew dai instead of sweet drinks. Avoid skipping meals or crash diets. [lg-05-eating-for-pre-diabetes][lg-01-healthy-plate] Since your glucose result is high, please arrange a doctor follow-up to confirm what it means and whether you need repeat testing or a personalised plan. [lg-08-screening-schedule]\",\"intent\":\"nutrition\",\"risk_level\":\"moderate\",\"route\":\"self_care\",\"cited_sources\":[\"lg-05-eating-for-pre-diabetes\",\"lg-01-healthy-plate\",\"lg-08-screening-schedule\"],\"personalisation_flags\":[\"high glucose screening result\",\"doctor follow-up advised\"]}\r\n"]
